{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the probability that at least two out of five fair six-sided dice show the same number, we can use the complementary probability approach. This means we first calculate the probability that all five dice show different numbers, and then subtract this from 1.\n\n1. **Calculate the probability that all five dice show different numbers:**\n\n   - The first die can show any of the 6 faces. So, there are 6 possible outcomes for the first die.\n   - The second die must show a different number from the first die, so there are 5 possible outcomes for the second die.\n   - The third die must show a different number from the first two dice, so there are 4 possible outcomes for the third die.\n   - The fourth die must show a different number from the first three dice, so there are 3 possible outcomes for the fourth die.\n   - The fifth die must show a different number from the first four dice, so there are 2 possible outcomes for the fifth die.\n\n","prefix_end":949,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,18927,429,518,3245,1378,700,315,4236,6624,4743,49758,22120,1473,279,1852,1372,11,582,646,990,279,57435,18927,5486,13,1096,3363,582,1156,11047,279,18927,429,678,4236,22120,1473,2155,5109,11,323,1221,32256,419,504,220,16,382,16,13,3070,47866,279,18927,429,678,4236,22120,1473,2155,5109,25,56177,256,481,576,1156,2746,646,1473,894,315,279,220,21,12300,13,2055,11,1052,525,220,21,3204,19554,369,279,1156,2746,624,256,481,576,2086,2746,1969,1473,264,2155,1372,504,279,1156,2746,11,773,1052,525,220,20,3204,19554,369,279,2086,2746,624,256,481,576,4843,2746,1969,1473,264,2155,1372,504,279,1156,1378,22120,11,773,1052,525,220,19,3204,19554,369,279,4843,2746,624,256,481,576,11737,2746,1969,1473,264,2155,1372,504,279,1156,2326,22120,11,773,1052,525,220,18,3204,19554,369,279,11737,2746,624,256,481,576,17702,2746,1969,1473,